name: Refused context work preserves the parent Review allowance
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_AGENT_MCPS
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/allowance_inheritance.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 parent Review allowance | refused-context
expect: Context investigation accounting
expect: no model request started
resize: 160x48
live-snap: refused-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: refused-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: refused-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: refused-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: refused-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: refusal-reading-40x12
keys: End
live-snap: refusal-tail-40x12
ask: Does this refusal explain that Context work cannot consume the parent Review allowance and give a deliberate next step without implying a paid request or a completed phase?
resize: 120x36
submit: logs
paste-file: @ART/allowance-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Calls committed: 0/1 | unchanged-allowance
expect: protected review remaining: 1
expect: Calls available for context, scopes, scans and lessons: 0
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/allowance_inheritance.py @TMP_TARGET @ART unchanged
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 parent Review allowance | restarted-refusal
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: restarted-refusal-tail-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/allowance_inheritance.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the refusal and untouched Review allocation with no automatic retry or new job?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
